  "task": "Each source has two targets: finite2 with new response parameters, or recurrent with the original response parameters. Both targets share paid prefix controls. Private family labels and seeds appear only in the experiment protocol/results.",
  "source": "The same source archive and five development tasks; only fresh-confirmation streams advance by 310009 + replica_index * 170003. Existing practice-index increments remain. No prior practice coverage or target outcomes enters author context.",
  "intervention": "Three independent authors start from the same unpublished candidate. Two existing programs are supplied under alternating neutral file names with compact source-only practice evidence. Authors may copy a program or edit locally, then request the unchanged five-case scoped publication gate. No automatic adoption.",
  "controller": "The author selects program edits, paid practice and publication. Each practice and transfer begins with 72 paid controls-only rows, then executes at most 12 declared program steps with 24-row fresh confirmation. All fits and observations share each episode's actual budgets. Transfer uses zero LLM calls; this is LLM-authored method execution, not online LLM selection of each action.",
  "archive_publication": "New predictors retain ordinary code, data and binary dependencies. Imported confirmed-model archives accompany them only when declared in the successful finish.reused_files. Runner logs and the undeclared candidate catalog are excluded. An unchanged directly submitted archive keeps its existing dependencies. Revisions to an inherited model publish a new candidate. A latest predictor explicitly depending on an older candidate retains that dependency, which is reported.",
  "failure_policy": "Exactly three registered author attempts, with no adaptive continuation or replacement of failures. Unpublished authors leave ten target slots skipped.",
  "accounting": "Charge every new author once and only newly executed targets. Report reused source evidence and target executions separately, without charging them again. Unknown model usage remains unknown.",
  "terminal_order": "Finish all authors and all newly required target research before terminal scoring. Target results are never supplied to authors or used for publication.",
  "scope": "Autonomous selection or local revision of supplied existing programs on familiar development tasks; not autonomous invention, unseen-family confirmation or broad reliability. A reused target outcome is historical evidence, not a new experiment.",
  "model_identity": "gpt-6-luna is requested through the existing subscription provider. Usage metadata repeating that name does not independently establish server routing.",
